; Lab 1, side effects: (inc! x) adds 1 to x and yields the new value. The language evaluates the left
; operand first, so x is read (5) before inc! runs: 5 + 6*2 = 17.
; The right operand needs more registers, so Sethi-Ullman ordering would like to evaluate it first.
(program
  (vars x)
  (body
    (set! x 5)
    (print (+ x (* (inc! x) 2)))
    (print x)))
